-- A cycle made in a `case` subject, which is no binder, lives until
-- `g`'s boundary, and there `r` and `s` carry two isomorphic cyclic records
-- that `[ r, s ]` unifies. Unification is coinductive (checker-v2.md §7.3):
-- the two cycles unify, and the boundary reports ONE `infinite_type`, at the
-- parameter `r` (§8.2). Recursing through two cyclic fields to the depth
-- guard would be exponential; the report is at the parameter, not the
-- body, and never `a  =  … a …`.
g r s =
    case [ r, { a = r, b = r } ] of
        _ →
            case [ s, { a = s, b = s } ] of
                _ →
                    [ r, s ]
